UPDATE goals SET description = 'The remaining members of the Company follow the Silverlode stream down from the mountains until the trees of the Golden Wood rise up to meet them. Legolas speaks of Lothlórien with reverence, yet Boromir fears the legends of the sorceress who dwells within. Stepping beneath the eaves, the travellers find the light has changed, no longer the grey of winter but a golden hue that seems trapped within the leaves. The air itself feels different here, healing and ancient, as the weariness of Moria begins to lift in the presence of an elder magic.' WHERE distance = 855 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Cross the Silverlode on ropes (Distance: 861)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'Guided by Haldir and his wardens, the Company reached the banks of the Silverlode, the river Celebrant, which flowed cold and swift from the mountains. To continue into the heart of the Golden Wood, the travellers had to cross the rushing water upon slender grey ropes strung between the great trees on either bank. Legolas moved across the swaying cord with elven grace, but for the hobbits, specifically Samwise, the crossing proved a terrified ordeal of clinging hands and shuffling feet. Once safely on the far side, they stood within the Naith of Lórien, surrounded by the towering mallorn-trees that would shelter them from the outside world.' WHERE distance = 861 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Reach the hill of Cerin Amroth (Distance: 906)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The Company walked through the open glades of the Golden Wood, marvelling at the mallorn-trees that towered like living pillars of silver and gold. As the path wound deeper into Lothlórien, the weary travellers approached a great mound covered in the pale winter flowers of niphredil and elanor. This was Cerin Amroth, the heart of the ancient realm, rising green and fair above the surrounding forest floor. Frodo felt a timeless peace wash over him, as if the shadow of the outside world had no power to touch this high and holy place.' WHERE distance = 906 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Reach Cerin Amroth and meet Celeborn and Galadriel (Distance: 920)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The travellers are led from the mound of Amroth to the great city of Caras Galadhon, a fortress of green towers illuminated by countless silver lamps. Climbing the white ladders of the mightiest mallorn, they are brought before the Lord Celeborn and the Lady Galadriel in their high chamber. In the Lady''s gaze, which seems deeper than the sea, each member of the Fellowship feels their mind searched and their secret desires laid bare. Here, amidst the ancient power of the Elves, the Company is granted sanctuary for a time, finding rest within the heart of the Golden Wood.' WHERE distance = 920 * 1.60934;

